From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WinZapp build <build@winzapp.invalid>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:15:03 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] send: the sender key only for the devices that do not hold it

Every group message encrypted the sender key distribution message for every
device of the group: one pairwise encryption and one session write per device,
and a node that grows with them. Measured with Neonize: 1250 ms for a reply to
a group of about 65 people and 3753 ms for a file, against 158 ms for a text
to a person. WhatsApp's own clients distribute the key once.

The client now remembers, in memory, the devices each group's key reached,
and leaves <participants> out when nobody needs it. A device that lost the key
asks with a retry receipt, which already answers with the key, and a send that
fails forgets the group, so its next message goes to everyone again.
